To decouple the Conversation Engine, Context Engine, and Application Orchestrator, you can create separate interfaces or classes for each engine. The Conversation Engine should have methods for sending messages and managing lineage. The Context Engine should have methods for selecting and budgeting references. The Application Orchestrator should have methods for coordinating the interactions between the three engines.

Here's an example of how you might define these interfaces:

```plaintext
// ConversationEngine interface
interface ConversationEngine {
  void sendMessage(Message message);
  void manageLineage(Message message);
}

// ContextEngine interface
interface ContextEngine {
  Reference selectReference();
  void budgetReference(Reference reference);
}

// ApplicationOrchestrator interface
interface ApplicationOrchestrator {
  void coordinateEngines();
}
```

You can then implement these interfaces in separate classes:

```plaintext
// ConversationEngine implementation
class ConversationEngineImpl implements ConversationEngine {
  @Override
  public void sendMessage(Message message) {
    // Implementation to send message
  }

  @Override
  public void manageLineage(Message message) {
    // Implementation to manage lineage
  }
}

// ContextEngine implementation
class ContextEngineImpl implements ContextEngine {
  @Override
  public Reference selectReference() {
    // Implementation to select reference
    return new Reference();
  }

  @Override
  public void budgetReference(Reference reference) {
    // Implementation to budget reference
  }
}

// ApplicationOrchestrator implementation
class ApplicationOrchestratorImpl implements ApplicationOrchestrator {
  @Override
  public void coordinateEngines() {
    // Implementation to coordinate engines
  }
}
```

Finally, you can use these interfaces to coordinate the interactions between the three engines:

```plaintext
// Example usage
ConversationEngine conversationEngine = new ConversationEngineImpl();
ContextEngine contextEngine = new ContextEngineImpl();
ApplicationOrchestrator applicationOrchestrator = new ApplicationOrchestratorImpl();

conversationEngine.sendMessage(new Message());
contextEngine.selectReference();
applicationOrchestrator.coordinateEngines();
```

By decoupling the Conversation Engine, Context Engine, and Application Orchestrator, you can make it easier to modify or replace each engine without affecting the others. This can also make it easier to test and debug each engine independently.

